      "reconstructed": "The literal finite real coordinate function space Fin n → ℝ, with its default Pi topology, supremum norm and Borel measurable structure. n ranges over all natural numbers, with no positive-dimension restriction. For n = 0 this is the singleton empty-coordinate space. Genuine L1 integrability under γ holds for x ↦ f(x)², x ↦ f(x)² Real.log(f(x)²), each x ↦ (D_i f(x))², and x ↦ Σ_i (D_i f(x))². In addition, ∫ f² Real.log(f²) dγ − (∫ f² dγ) Real.log(∫ f² dγ) ≤ 2 ∫ Σ_i (D_i f)² dγ. The constant 2 is independent of n and f.",
